└── Python style guide checker / linter plugin base
    ├── Candidates : pep8, pycodestyle, flake8, ruff
    ├── Used APIs  : noqa
    ├── Pitfalls   : pep8 package is unmaintained since 2016; pycodestyle is the direct 
    │   successor; flake8 and ruff are full linters with plugin ecosystems, not just style 
    │   checkers; ruff is written in Rust and significantly faster but has different 
    │   configuration format; flake8 requires plugins for some checks that pycodestyle 
    │   handles natively
    └── pep8 was renamed to pycodestyle in 2016; both provide the same noqa() function for 
        inline ignore comments. flake8 and ruff are modern linters that also understand # 
        noqa comments and can serve as drop-in replacements for the linting role. The code 
        only uses pep8.noqa() to check for noqa comments, which all candidates support.

